{
  "id": "V23",
  "title": "Deflection distribution — a wall with no story shear (rotated by the stack above)",
  "intent": "Two stories, two walls each (8 ft and 4 ft), 1.0E = 5 k at Level 2. The upper short wall SW-4 is stiffer than SW-3 for its length (2\" o.c. both sides vs 6\" o.c.), so it takes a large part of Level 2 and sends a large end force down onto the lower short wall SW-6. With that force alone, SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1 already gives SW-6 more deflection than SW-5 deflects carrying the whole story. No equal-δ split with positive shares exists: SW-6 takes no story shear (user rule: zero share + warning), SW-5 takes all 5 k, and the tool warns: SW-6 with its holdown check and the other fixes, and — the big warning — SW-5 carrying more than it is designed for, because at equal δ SW-6 would push back.",
  "covers": [
    "Deflection distribution (equal δ, Σ V = V)",
    "SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1 with the end forces from above",
    "Zero-share wall warning + holdown check (F-DD1)",
    "Free split — walls carrying more than designed"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Every wall uses SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1 at 1.0E: δ = 8vh³/(EAb) + vh/(1000G_a) + (h/b)·(δ_cap·T/P_δ + Δ_c(r)), v = 1000V/b, T = C = 1000·V·h/b + the end force from above (lb). P_δ = HDUE cap, MSTC cap/0.7; r = C/(A·625). Pinned: SW-3 6\" o.c. (G_a 16), SW-4 / SW-5 / SW-6 2\" o.c. both sides (G_a 56); SW-3 / SW-4 MSTC66 + (3)2x4; SW-5 HDUE13 + 8x4; SW-6 HDUE5 + (2)2x4."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Level 2 (nothing above), equal δ: V_3 = 3.073 k, V_4 = 1.927 k, δ = 0.3423 in. SW-4 takes 38.54 % of Level 2 on 33.33 % of the length. End forces sent down (1.0E): SW-3 → SW-5 T = 3841 lb, SW-4 → SW-6 T = 4817 lb."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "SW-6 at zero own share (only the force from SW-4): slip = 0.146 × 4817 / 5375 = 0.1308 in, crushing Δ_c = 0.0203 in → δ_6(0) = (10/4) × (0.1308 + 0.0203) = 0.3779 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-5 carrying the whole story (V = 5 k, plus 3841 lb from SW-3): 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0140, vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1116, h·Δa/b = 0.1623 → δ_5(5 k) = 0.2879 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "δ_6(0) = 0.3779 in > δ_5(5 k) = 0.2879 in: even with no shear of its own SW-6 is displaced more than SW-5 carrying all of Level 1. No split with equal δ and V ≥ 0 exists → SW-6 takes 0, SW-5 takes 5 k, story δ = 0.2879 in; SW-6 is flagged (zero share). Its drift δ is its zero-share value 0.3779 in (the larger)."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Holdown check (both ends, post raised to the HDUE minimum post, SW-5 held): HDUE7 + (2)2x4: δ_6(0) = 0.3151 in → share 0.000 k; HDUE9 + 4x4: δ_6(0) = 0.2704 in → share 0.069 k; HDUE13 + 8x4: δ_6(0) = 0.1550 in → share 0.733 k; HDUE17 + 6x4: δ_6(0) = 0.1030 in → share 1.166 k. HDUE7 is not enough (δ_6(0) > 0.2879 in); the lightest giving a share is HDUE9 (0.069 k, barely), HDUE13 gives 0.733 k. Other fixes (listed, not calculated by the tool): a longer SW-6, less force from the stack above, or a less stiff SW-5 (its strength needs only 4\" o.c.: 0.7 × 5000 / 8 = 438 plf ≤ 470)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Free split (equal δ without the V ≥ 0 limit, information only; T and C clipped at 0): δ_5(V_5) = δ_6(V − V_5) → V_5 = 5.285 k, V_6 = -0.285 k (SW-6 pushes back), δ = 0.3008 in. SW-5 is designed for 5.000 k but would carry 5.285 k (+5.70 %) → big warning: check SW-5, more wall may be needed. The design keeps the zero share (user rule 2026-10-01)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Story drift (Cd = 4, Ie = 1.0, RC II → Δa = 0.020 × h_sx = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in): Level 2 δxe = 0.3423 in (equal δ) → δx = 4 × 0.3423 / 1.0 = 1.3691 in ≤ 2.400 OK; Level 1 δxe = the larger wall δ = SW-6 at zero share 0.3779 in → δx = 1.5114 in ≤ 2.400 OK. No drift sizing (design pinned). Ω₀ = 2.5 only adds the Ω₀ force tables (not used for design)."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Line checks: G3 shows Σ shares = 5 k, SW-5 δ = story δ, and SW-6 δ(0) ≥ story δ; G1–G12 pass."
    }
  ],
